TASK SPECIFICATIONS:
{
  "id": "PUB009",
  "title": "Calculate Moving Average",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "requirements": "# Calculate Moving Average\n\n- **Difficulty:** Medium (medium)\n\n## Requirements\n\nWrite a function block FB that calculates and updates a moving arithmetic mean. The moving arithmetic mean is a method of averaging over consecutive data points, where each new data point replaces the oldest data point, and then the average is recalculated.\n\n1. When cyclicExecution is TRUE, a new data value is automatically read and the moving average average is updated every scan cycle.\n2. Provide an external trigger signal trigger, which reads a new data value and updates the moving average upon each rising edge.\n3. Provide a reset function reset, which resets the moving average calculation when the reset signal is TRUE. If the window size is less than 1 or greater than 100, output an error status and status code.\n\nThe status parameter indicates the execution status of the program:\n- 16#0000: Execution successful\n- 16#8200: Window length setting error, please set a value between 1 and 100.\n\n## Interface Definition\n\n| Direction | Variable/Field | Data Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Input | `cyclicExecution` | `BOOL` | When TRUE, periodic reading is performed, and trigger has no effect |\n| Input | `trigger` | `BOOL` | External trigger signal, reads value upon each rising edge |\n| Input | `value` | `LREAL` | Newly read data value |\n| Input | `windowSize` | `INT` | The window size for the moving average, which must be between 1 and 100 |\n| Input | `reset` | `BOOL` | Reset signal, resets the moving average calculation when TRUE |\n| Output | `average` | `LREAL` | The moving average |\n| Output | `windowSizeReached` | `BOOL` | FALSE: Maximum window width not yet reached TRUE: Maximum window width has been reached |\n| Output | `error` | `BOOL` | FALSE: No error occurred TRUE: An error occurred during the execution of FB |\n| Output | `status` | `WORD` | Status code |",
  "scenario": "Write a function block FB that calculates and updates a moving arithmetic mean. The moving arithmetic mean is a method of averaging over consecutive data points, where each new data point replaces the oldest data point, and then the average is recalculated.",
  "interface": [
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "cyclicExecution",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "When TRUE, periodic reading is performed, and trigger has no effect"
    },
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "trigger",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "External trigger signal, reads value upon each rising edge"
    },
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "value",
      "type": "LREAL",
      "description": "Newly read data value"
    },
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "windowSize",
      "type": "INT",
      "description": "The window size for the moving average, which must be between 1 and 100"
    },
    {
      "direction": "INPUT",
      "name": "reset",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "Reset signal, resets the moving average calculation when TRUE"
    },
    {
      "direction": "OUTPUT",
      "name": "average",
      "type": "LREAL",
      "description": "The moving average"
    },
    {
      "direction": "OUTPUT",
      "name": "windowSizeReached",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "FALSE: Maximum window width not yet reached TRUE: Maximum window width has been reached"
    },
    {
      "direction": "OUTPUT",
      "name": "error",
      "type": "BOOL",
      "description": "FALSE: No error occurred TRUE: An error occurred during the execution of FB"
    },
    {
      "direction": "OUTPUT",
      "name": "status",
      "type": "WORD",
      "description": "Status code"
    }
  ],
  "initial_conditions": {
    "average": 0.0,
    "windowSizeReached": false,
    "error": false,
    "status": 0,
    "sampleCount": 0,
    "previousTrigger": false
  },
  "scan_semantics": "At scan k, inputs I[k] are sampled once, q[k] is pre-scan retained state, outputs O[k] are observed after execution, and q[k+1] is the updated state. Each test creates a fresh FB instance before step 0. An initialized instance has not yet executed a scan. Timer elapsed time is zero on the first eligible sampled invocation; dt_ms is elapsed wall time since the previous invocation, not automatically a synthetic input to the FB. No unobserved past input stability is assumed. All sequences here are expected values.",
  "safety_priority": [
    "Invalid window returns an error before sampling.",
    "Reset overrides sample acceptance.",
    "Cyclic and trigger conditions cannot cause double insertion."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "During warm-up, average is the mean of the actual accepted samples; zero-filled unused capacity is excluded.",
    "reset has priority over sampling for a valid window; it clears history and sets average=0 and windowSizeReached=FALSE.",
    "Changing a valid windowSize clears history before any same-scan accepted sample. Invalid window sets error/status and does not accept or change history.",
    "An invalid-window scan preserves average/windowSizeReached. Returning to a valid window clears error/status. Trigger edge history is updated on every invocation, including reset and invalid-window scans.",
    "cyclicExecution accepts exactly one sample per scan and ignores the trigger. windowSizeReached becomes TRUE once the accepted sample count reaches windowSize.",
    "The task interface, requirements, assumptions, and normalized LTL definitions (excluding reference-only ground truth) are supplied identically to both frameworks. Output names always denote observed candidate outputs, never precomputed expected values.",
    "Floating-point inputs and intermediate reference arithmetic are finite. Existing fixed traces retain their declared absolute tolerance; claims do not extend to arbitrary magnitudes without a separately specified numeric error policy.",
    "LREAL average comparisons allow up to abs<=1e-5 (and matching relative precision on T2). P6 initializes previousTrigger=FALSE prior to scan k=0.",
    "The task interface, requirements, assumptions, and normalized LTL definitions (excluding reference-only ground truth) are supplied identically to both frameworks. Output names always denote observed candidate outputs, never precomputed expected values."
  ],
  "ltl": [
    {
      "id": "PUB009.P_init",
      "kind": "safety",
      "formula": "init",
      "description": "Before the first scan invocation, all declared OUTPUT variables and initial instance state hold their declared initial values.",
      "explanation": "Applies strictly to the fresh pre-invocation initial instance observation before scan k=0 (INITIAL_INSTANCE scope).",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "INITIAL_INSTANCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB009.P1",
      "formula": "G(!valid -> (error & status=16#8200 & unchangedMean))",
      "explanation": "Window bounds are checked without silently accepting data.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB009.P2",
      "formula": "G(valid -> (!error & status=0))",
      "explanation": "A valid window clears configuration error.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB009.P3",
      "formula": "G((valid & reset) -> (average=0 & !windowSizeReached))",
      "explanation": "Reset produces an empty history.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB009.P4",
      "formula": "G((valid & !reset) -> average=meanOrZero(historyAfter))",
      "explanation": "The result is the arithmetic mean of the active window or zero when empty.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB009.P5",
      "formula": "G(valid -> (windowSizeReached <-> length(historyAfter)=windowSize))",
      "explanation": "Full-window indication follows history population.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB009.P6",
      "formula": "G(trigger <-> X(previousTrigger))",
      "explanation": "Both operands are Boolean propositions. previousTrigger[0]=FALSE; previousTrigger[k+1]=I[k].trigger on every invocation, including invalid/reset.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    },
    {
      "id": "PUB009.P7",
      "formula": "G((valid & !reset & !cyclicExecution & !triggerRise & !windowChanged) -> unchangedMean)",
      "explanation": "No event means no sample update.",
      "language": "LTL_OVER_TYPED_SCAN_PREDICATES",
      "encoding_status": "NOT_LOWERED_TO_MODEL_CHECKER",
      "scope": "SCAN_SEQUENCE"
    }
  ],
  "atomic_propositions": {
    "valid": "1<=windowSize<=100",
    "triggerRise": "trigger & !previousTrigger",
    "accept": "valid & !reset & (cyclicExecution | triggerRise)",
    "history": "Ghost ordered list of at most windowSize accepted samples, newest last.",
    "historyAfter": "history after clearing on reset/window change and adding one accepted sample, discarding oldest if full.",
    "unchangedMean": "average and windowSizeReached equal their pre-scan values.",
    "interface names": "Identically named sampled input or observed output.",
    "meanOrZero": "Arithmetic mean for a nonempty list, otherwise zero.",
    "length": "Number of samples in the history list.",
    "windowChanged": "Current valid windowSize differs from the last valid configured size.",
    "previousTrigger": "{\"kind\": \"previous_sampled_input\", \"source\": \"I[k-1].trigger\", \"initial\": false, \"update\": \"After EVERY scan k, including invalid/reset/stop, store I[k].trigger\"}",
    "cyclicExecution": "I[k].cyclicExecution: sampled input (BOOL).",
    "trigger": "I[k].trigger: sampled input (BOOL).",
    "value": "I[k].value: sampled input (LREAL).",
    "windowSize": "I[k].windowSize: sampled input (INT).",
    "reset": "I[k].reset: sampled input (BOOL).",
    "average": "O[k].average: independently observed post-scan candidate value (LREAL); never defined as expected output.",
    "windowSizeReached": "O[k].windowSizeReached: independently observed post-scan candidate value (BOOL); never defined as expected output.",
    "error": "O[k].error: independently observed post-scan candidate value (BOOL); never defined as expected output.",
    "status": "O[k].status: independently observed post-scan candidate value (WORD); never defined as expected output.",
    "init": "At the separate pre-invocation initial observation before scan k=0: O_init.average=0.0, O_init.windowSizeReached=false, O_init.error=false, O_init.status=0."
  }
}

ARCHITECTURAL PLAN:
{
  "state_machine": [
    {
      "state": "EMPTY",
      "condition": "Valid configuration with sampleCount = 0; also the initial state."
    },
    {
      "state": "FILLING",
      "condition": "Valid configuration with 0 < sampleCount < activeWindowSize."
    },
    {
      "state": "FULL",
      "condition": "Valid configuration with sampleCount = activeWindowSize > 0."
    },
    {
      "state": "INVALID_WINDOW",
      "condition": "windowSize < 1 or windowSize > 100; history and mean are retained."
    },
    {
      "transitions": [
        "From any state, an invalid window enters INVALID_WINDOW without changing calculation history or activeWindowSize.",
        "On a valid scan, update activeWindowSize. If reset is TRUE or the valid size changed, clear the history before considering sampling.",
        "On a valid scan with reset FALSE, accept exactly one value if cyclicExecution is TRUE or triggerRise is TRUE; otherwise accept none.",
        "After valid-scan actions, enter EMPTY, FILLING, or FULL according to sampleCount and activeWindowSize. This also governs recovery from INVALID_WINDOW."
      ],
      "history_algorithm": "Use a 100-element circular buffer and a zero-based nextIndex. Clearing sets sampleCount and nextIndex to zero and mean to 0.0. On acceptance, write value at nextIndex, increment sampleCount up to activeWindowSize, advance nextIndex modulo activeWindowSize, and calculate the arithmetic mean of the sampleCount active elements. Once full, the write replaces the oldest element.",
      "numeric_policy": "Use LREAL arithmetic. Check results against the specified trace tolerances; no accuracy guarantee is claimed for arbitrary magnitudes beyond the supplied finite-arithmetic assumptions."
    }
  ],
  "timer_plan": {
    "timers": [],
    "PT_durations": "None",
    "reset_conditions": "Not applicable; sampling is scan-driven or edge-triggered."
  },
  "priorities": [
    "Invalid window detection overrides reset and sampling: report 16#8200 and preserve history, average, and windowSizeReached.",
    "For a valid window, reset overrides sampling and clears history. Record the current valid window size even during reset.",
    "A changed valid window clears history before any same-scan accepted sample. The first valid size is treated as a change from the initial sentinel.",
    "Cyclic execution accepts one sample per valid, non-reset scan; trigger cannot cause a second insertion.",
    "Update trigger edge history on every invocation, including cyclic, reset, and invalid-window scans."
  ],
  "initial_values": {
    "average": 0.0,
    "windowSizeReached": false,
    "error": false,
    "status": "16#0000",
    "sampleCount": 0,
    "previousTrigger": false,
    "activeWindowSize": 0,
    "nextIndex": 0,
    "mean": 0.0,
    "sampleBuffer": {
      "length": 100,
      "element_initial_value": 0.0
    },
    "state": "EMPTY"
  },
  "scan_execution_order": [
    {
      "stage": 1,
      "name": "Edge sampling",
      "actions": [
        "Sample all inputs once.",
        "Compute triggerRise = trigger AND NOT previousTrigger, then store the sampled trigger in previousTrigger unconditionally."
      ]
    },
    {
      "stage": 2,
      "name": "Safety/reset priority and state transitions",
      "actions": [
        "Check windowSize bounds. If invalid, preserve calculation state and select INVALID_WINDOW.",
        "If valid, detect a change from activeWindowSize and record the current size. Clear history on reset or size change.",
        "If valid and reset is FALSE, accept one sample when cyclicExecution OR triggerRise is TRUE; update the circular buffer, count, and mean.",
        "Select EMPTY, FILLING, or FULL from the resulting count."
      ]
    },
    {
      "stage": 3,
      "name": "Unconditional top-level timer FB calls outside CASE/IF",
      "actions": [
        "No timer FBs are required; this stage is a no-op."
      ]
    },
    {
      "stage": 4,
      "name": "Unified output assignments",
      "actions": [
        "Assign average from the retained mean.",
        "Assign windowSizeReached = (activeWindowSize > 0 AND sampleCount = activeWindowSize); retained calculation state preserves this output during invalid scans.",
        "Assign error and status from the sampled window validity: invalid gives TRUE and 16#8200; valid gives FALSE and 16#0000."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "formal_assertions": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "formula": "G((windowSize < 1 OR windowSize > 100) -> (error AND status = 16#8200))"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "formula": "G((windowSize >= 1 AND windowSize <= 100) -> (NOT error AND status = 16#0000))"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "formula": "G((windowSize >= 1 AND windowSize <= 100 AND reset) -> (average = 0.0 AND NOT windowSizeReached))"
    }
  ]
}

CODESYS DIALECT CARDS:
[
  {
    "id": "edge_detection",
    "title": "Edge Detection (R_TRIG, F_TRIG and Manual Pattern)",
    "body": "// R_TRIG / F_TRIG function blocks and manual edge detection pattern\nVAR\n    rTrig : R_TRIG;\n    prevSignal : BOOL;\n    rising : BOOL;\nEND_VAR\nrTrig(CLK := rawSignal); // rTrig.Q is TRUE for one scan on rising edge\n// Manual edge pattern:\nrising := rawSignal AND NOT prevSignal;\nprevSignal := rawSignal;"
  },
  {
    "id": "ton_timer",
    "title": "Standard IEC TON Timer Block Invocation",
    "body": "// Standard IEC TON timer: MUST invoke unconditionally OUTSIDE CASE/IF every scan!\nVAR\n    timer : TON;\n    runTimer : BOOL;\nEND_VAR\n// Control via boolean IN flag (never put timer(...) only inside an IF/CASE arm):\nrunTimer := (state = 1) AND NOT resetCmd;\ntimer(IN := runTimer, PT := T#2s);\nIF timer.Q THEN\n    // Timer expired; timer.ET holds elapsed time\nEND_IF;"
  },
  {
    "id": "case_state_machine",
    "title": "Explicit CASE State Machine Transitions",
    "body": "// 4-Stage Scan Order: 1) Edge sample 2) Reset/priority & CASE state transition\n// 3) Unconditional top-level TON/R_TRIG calls 4) Unified output assignments\nVAR\n    state : INT := 0; // 0=IDLE, 1=RUN, 2=FAULT\nEND_VAR\nIF emergencyStop THEN state := 2; END_IF;\nCASE state OF\n    0: IF startCmd AND NOT fault THEN state := 1; END_IF;\n    1: IF faultCmd THEN state := 2; ELSIF stopCmd THEN state := 0; END_IF;\n    2: IF resetCmd THEN state := 0; END_IF;\n    ELSE state := 0;\nEND_CASE;\noutActive := (state = 1); // Assign outputs unconditionally from current state"
  }
]

